; Repeat the previous command (the @ key)
;
; Reached from the line editor #R$6DD6 when "@" is the first key of an empty
; line. The input line buffer still holds the previous line and the parsed
; word list at $709C is untouched, so the caller only has to parse that list
; again: this routine rubs out the "> " prompt with two back-spaces and
; returns Z with A = 0, which sends the caller (#R$6C00) straight to parsing.
; .
; While a question of the game ("Which ...?") waits for its answer
; (AwaitingAnswer is not 0) the key is ignored and the editor goes on reading keys.
; .
; Hardware: echoes through #R$858B (input window).
;
; O:A 0
; O:F Z set (no new line was typed)
c$6E7A LD A,($B71A)  ; AwaitingAnswer: an answer is awaited
 $6E7D AND A         ;
 $6E7E JP NZ,$6DF5   ; yes: ignore "@", read the next key
@isub=LD A,CHAR_BACKSPACE
 $6E81 LD A,$08      ;
 $6E83 CALL $858B    ; rub out the prompt ">"
 $6E86 CALL $858B    ; and the space after it
 $6E89 XOR A         ;
 $6E8A RET           ;
